@switch INTERACT_VERB
@case "look"
	It's dusty, with a badly-worn spine.
@case "take"
	Doesn't seem important enough to take.
@case "read"
	@switch book_number
		@case 1
			"The first of his line was the fearsome Azarin."
			"With a heart and scales of gold, he built and defended the venerable hall."
		@case 2
			"Second in the line was Azarin's son, Dron."
			"Those who met with the gaze of his emerald eyes were swiftly eviscerated."
		@case 3
			"The third heir was the draconic witch, Morganthe."
			"Her dark magicks and steel claws tore intruders asunder with a crimson flourish."
		@case 4
			"The fourth heir was a kind dragon clad in azure scales, Nyriti."
			"She loved to sing, and her voice captivated many an audience."
		@case 5
			"Anu Revisla, guardian of dreams, was the fifth to the throne."
			"Though he dreamed of a lush green future, ruin sadly fell upon his family."
		@case 6
			"The last of her line is the Scarlet Reaver, Thelana."
			"She oversees the hall to this day, with quiet resolve."
@case else
	Cannot do.
